# shadcn MCP + shared `packages/ui`

## Enable the server

In **Cursor Settings → MCP**, ensure the **shadcn** server is on for this workspace. The project config lives at [`.cursor/mcp.json`](.cursor/mcp.json) (also includes **Context7**). The shadcn server uses **`--cwd packages/ui`** so new primitives land in [`packages/ui`](packages/ui) (see [`packages/ui/components.json`](packages/ui/components.json)). The Vite POS app still has local `apps/pos-frontend/components.json` for legacy primitives; prefer the shared package for new work.

## Prefer MCP over guessing

When adding or changing shared UI, **use the shadcn MCP tools** (same registry as `npx shadcn@latest add`):

1. **`get_project_registries`** — Confirm registries (e.g. `@shadcn`) from `components.json`.
2. **`search_items_in_registries`** — Fuzzy search; pass `registries` like `["@shadcn"]` and a `query` (e.g. `sidebar`, `data table`, `form`).
3. **`list_items_in_registries`** — Browse a registry when you do not have a specific query.
4. **`view_items_in_registries`** — Inspect an item (e.g. `@shadcn/button`) before adding.
5. **`get_item_examples_from_registries`** — Pull demos/examples (e.g. `sidebar-demo`, `card example`).
6. **`get_add_command_for_items`** — Get the exact **`npx shadcn@latest add …`** command; run it **from `packages/ui`** so files land under `packages/ui/src/components/ui` and aliases match.
7. **`get_audit_checklist`** — Run after adding components to catch imports, deps, and lint issues.

Do **not** recreate primitives that exist in the registry (sidebar, sheet, dialog, table, form, etc.) with one-off `div` layouts unless there is no suitable registry item.

## CLI parity

MCP **`get_add_command_for_items`** and **`npx shadcn@latest add <name> -y`** in `packages/ui` are equivalent for installation. Prefer MCP in chat so the assistant searches registries and examples first.
